3100`: health `200`, create `201`, list `200`, get `200`, update `200`, delete `204`, deleted get `404`.\n- Validation checks on `POST /bookmarks`: missing title `400`, missing url `400`, empty title `400`.\n- Direct SQLite check confirmed the `bookmarks` schema and a persisted row in `data.db`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
./benchmark/runs/phase-3-active-observability-cli-1.4.1-rerun-20260531/T5-bug-fix/events.jsonl:39:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' docs/stories/US-003-folder-support.md\"","aggregated_output":"# US-003 Folder Support\n\n## Status\n\nimplemented\n\n## Lane\n\nnormal\n\n## Product Contract\n\nUsers can create, list, read, update, and delete folders. Bookmarks may optionally reference a folder, and deleting a folder leaves its bookmarks in place with `folder_id` set to `null`.\n\n## Relevant Product Docs\n\n- `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`\n- `docs/product/bookmarks.md`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- `POST /folders` creates a folder from required `name` and returns `201`.\n- `GET /folders` returns `200` with an array of folders.\n- `GET /folders/:id` returns `200` with a folder plus its `bookmarks` array, or `404`.\n- `PUT /folders/:id` updates folder `name` and returns `200`, or `404`.\n- `DELETE /folders/:id` returns `204`, or `404`, and nullifies matching bookmark `folder_id` values.\n- `POST /bookmarks` and `PUT /bookmarks/:id` accept optional `folder_id`.\n- Non-existent bookmark `folder_id` values return `400`.\n- Existing bookmark endpoints continue to work.\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Commands: create, update, delete folders; create/update bookmarks with optional folder reference.\n- Queries: list folders, fetch folder by id, fetch bookmarks for folder, validate folder existence.\n- API: Express JSON handlers under `/folders` plus updated `/bookmarks` handlers.\n- Tables: SQLite `folders` table; nullable `bookmarks.folder_id` foreign key.\n- Domain rules: folder `name` must be a non-empty string; `folder_id` must be `null`, omitted, or an existing positive integer folder id.\n- UI surfaces: none.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Layer | Expected proof |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unit | TypeScript build catches route/database typing issues. |\n| Integration | Local HTTP checks cover folder CRUD, bookmark folder assignment, invalid folder validation, delete nullification, and bookmark regression. |\n| E2E | Not applicable; API-only task. |\n| Platform | Not applicable beyond local Node/SQLite runtime. |\n| Release | Not applicable. |\n\n## Harness Delta\n\nAdded a story packet for the T3 folder support slice.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `npm run build`\n- Manual local HTTP checks on `PORT=3100`: create folder `201`, create bookmark with `folder_id` `201`, get folder with one bookmark `200`, update folder `200`, list folders array `200`, invalid `folder_id` `400`, bookmark list regression `200`, delete folder `204`, deleted folder bookmark `folder_id` became `null`, bookmark validation regressions `400`, health `200`.\n- `benchmark/lib/check-functional.sh` T3 check: create folder, list folders, get folder, create bookmark with folder, and bookmark list regression all passed.\n- `npm test` currently exits with code 1 because no Vitest test files exist.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
./benchmark/runs/phase-3-active-observability-cli-1.4.1-rerun-20260531/T5-bug-fix/events.jsonl:42:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '261,620p' src/index.ts\"","aggregated_output":"}\n\nfunction validateAuthBody(body: AuthBody): { value?: { email: string; password: string }; error?: string } {\n  const email = normalizeEmail(body.email);\n  if (!email) {\n    return { error: \"email must be a valid email address\" };\n  }\n\n  const password = normalizePassword(body.password);\n  if (!password) {\n    return { error: \"password must be at least 8 characters\" };\n  }\n\n  return { value: { email, password } };\n}\n\nfunction toPublicUser(user: User): PublicUser {\n  return {\n    id: user.id,\n    email: user.email,\n    created_at: user.created_at,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction createToken(userId: number): string {\n  return jwt.sign({ userId }, JWT_SECRET);\n}\n\nfunction getAuthenticatedUserId(req: Request): number {\n  return (req as unknown as AuthenticatedRequest).userId;\n}\n\nfunction authenticate(req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction): void {\n  const authorization = req.header(\"Authorization\");\n  if (!authorization?.startsWith(\"Bearer \")) {\n    res.status(401).json({ error: \"unauthorized\" });\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const token = authorization.slice(\"Bearer \".length).trim();\n  try {\n    const payload = jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET);\n    if (typeof payload !== \"object\" || typeof payload.userId !== \"number\") {\n      res.status(401).json({ error: \"unauthorized\" });\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const user = getUserById.get(payload.userId);\n    if (!user) {\n      res.status(401).json({ error: \"unauthorized\" });\n      return;\n    }\n\n    (req as AuthenticatedRequest).userId = payload.userId;\n    next();\n  } catch {\n    res.status(401).json({ error: \"unauthorized\" });\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateCreateBookmark(\n  body: BookmarkBody,\n  userId: number,\n): { v