./benchmark/runs/phase-3-active-observability-cli-1.4.1-rerun-20260531/T4-authentication/events.jsonl:37:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/product/bookmarks.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Bookmarks\n\nBookmarks are saved URLs with a title, optional description, optional folder, and creation/update timestamps. Folders are named collections of bookmarks.\n\n## API Contract\n\n- `POST /bookmarks` creates a bookmark from `url`, `title`, optional `description`, and optional `folder_id`.\n- `GET /bookmarks` returns all bookmarks as a JSON array.\n- `GET /bookmarks/:id` returns one bookmark or `404` when it does not exist.\n- `PUT /bookmarks/:id` updates an existing bookmark, including optional `folder_id`, and returns it, or `404` when it does not exist.\n- `DELETE /bookmarks/:id` removes an existing bookmark and returns `204`, or `404` when it does not exist.\n- `POST /folders` creates a folder from required `name` and returns `201`.\n- `GET /folders` returns all folders as a JSON array.\n- `GET /folders/:id` returns one folder with a `bookmarks` array or `404` when it does not exist.\n- `PUT /folders/:id` updates an existing folder name and returns it, or `404` when it does not exist.\n- `DELETE /folders/:id` removes a folder and returns `204`, or `404` when it does not exist. Bookmarks in the deleted folder are not deleted; their `folder_id` becomes `null`.\n\n## Data Contract\n\nBookmark records are stored in SQLite `data.db` in the `bookmarks` table:\n\n- `id`: integer primary key\n- `url`: required text\n- `title`: required text\n- `description`: nullable text\n- `folder_id`: nullable integer foreign key to `folders.id`\n- `created_at`: ISO timestamp text\n- `updated_at`: ISO timestamp text\n\nFolder records are stored in SQLite `data.db` in the `folders` table:\n\n- `id`: integer primary key\n- `name`: required text\n- `created_at`: ISO timestamp text\n- `updated_at`: ISO timestamp text\n\n## Validation\n\n- `url` is required for creation and must be a valid URL.\n- `title` is required for creation and must be a non-empty string.\n- Empty titles are rejected with `400`.\n- `folder_id`, when provided, must reference an existing folder or the request returns `400`.\n- Folder `name` is required and must be a non-empty string.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
./benchmark/runs/phase-3-active-observability-cli-1.4.1-rerun-20260531/T4-authentication/events.jsonl:39:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/stories/US-003-folder-support.md\"","aggregated_output":"# US-003 Folder Support\n\n## Status\n\nimplemented\n\n## Lane\n\nnormal\n\n## Product Contract\n\nUsers can create, list, read, update, and delete folders. Bookmarks may optionally reference a folder, and deleting a folder leaves its bookmarks in place with `folder_id` set to `null`.\n\n## Relevant Product Docs\n\n- `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`\n- `docs/product/bookmarks.md`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- `POST /folders` creates a folder from required `name` and returns `201`.\n- `GET /folders` returns `200` with an array of folders.\n- `GET /folders/:id` returns `200` with a folder plus its `bookmarks` array, or `404`.\n- `PUT /folders/:id` updates folder `name` and returns `200`, or `404`.\n- `DELETE /folders/:id` returns `204`, or `404`, and nullifies matching bookmark `folder_id` values.\n- `POST /bookmarks` and `PUT /bookmarks/:id` accept optional `folder_id`.\n- Non-existent bookmark `folder_id` values return `400`.\n- Existing bookmark endpoints continue to work.\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Commands: create, update, delete folders; create/update bookmarks with optional folder reference.\n- Queries: list folders, fetch folder by id, fetch bookmarks for folder, validate folder existence.\n- API: Express JSON handlers under `/folders` plus updated `/bookmarks` handlers.\n- Tables: SQLite `folders` table; nullable `bookmarks.folder_id` foreign key.\n- Domain rules: folder `name` must be a non-empty string; `folder_id` must be `null`, omitted, or an existing positive integer folder id.\n- UI surfaces: none.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Layer | Expected proof |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unit | TypeScript build catches route/database typing issues. |\n| Integration | Local HTTP checks cover folder CRUD, bookmark folder assignment, invalid folder validation, delete nullification, and bookmark regression. |\n| E2E | Not applicable; API-only task. |\n| Platform | Not applicable beyond local Node/SQLite runtime. |\n| Release | Not applicable. |\n\n## Harness Delta\n\nAdded a story packet for the T3 folder support slice.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `npm run build`\n- Manual local HTTP checks on `PORT=3100`: create folder `201`, create bookmark with `folder_id` `201`, get folder with one bookmark `200`, update folder `200`, list folders array `200`, invalid `folder_id` `400`, bookmark list regression `200`, delete folder `204`, deleted folder bookmark `folder_id` became `null`, bookmark validation regressions `400`, health `200`.\n- `benchmark/lib/check-functional.sh` T3 check: create folder, list folders, get folder, create bookmark with folder, and bookmark list regression all passed.\n- `npm test` currently exits with code 1 because no Vitest test files exist.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
