./benchmark/runs/phase-3-active-observability-cli-1.4.1-rerun-20260531/T6-pagination/events.jsonl:103:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/product/bookmarks.md | sed -n '1,90p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Bookmarks\n     2\t\n     3\tBookmarks are saved URLs with a title, optional description, optional folder, and creation/update timestamps. Folders are named collections of bookmarks. Users own their bookmarks and folders.\n     4\t\n     5\t## API Contract\n     6\t\n     7\t- `POST /auth/register` creates a user from valid `email` and `password`, stores a password hash, and returns the user without `password_hash`.\n     8\t- `POST /auth/login` authenticates a user from valid `email` and `password` and returns a JWT token.\n     9\t- All `/bookmarks` and `/folders` endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and return `401` when the token is missing or invalid.\n    10\t- `POST /bookmarks` creates an authenticated user's bookmark from `url`, `title`, optional `description`, and optional `folder_id`.\n    11\t- `GET /bookmarks` returns the authenticated user's bookmarks in a paginated JSON envelope: `{ \"data\": [...], \"page\": 1, \"limit\": 20, \"total\": 45 }`.\n    12\t- `GET /bookmarks/:id` returns one owned bookmark or `404` when it does not exist for that user.\n    13\t- `PUT /bookmarks/:id` updates an owned bookmark, including optional `folder_id`, and returns it, or `404` when it does not exist for that user.\n    14\t- `DELETE /bookmarks/:id` removes an owned bookmark and returns `204`, or `404` when it does not exist for that user.\n    15\t- `POST /folders` creates an authenticated user's folder from required `name` and returns `201`.\n    16\t- `GET /folders` returns the authenticated user's folders as a JSON array.\n    17\t- `GET /folders/:id` returns one owned folder with a `bookmarks` array or `404` when it does not exist for that user.\n    18\t- `PUT /folders/:id` updates an owned folder name and returns it, or `404` when it does not exist for that user.\n    19\t- `DELETE /folders/:id` removes an owned folder and returns `204`, or `404` when it does not exist for that user. Owned bookmarks in the deleted folder are not deleted; their `folder_id` becomes `null`.\n    20\t\n    21\t## Authentication\n    22\t\n    23\t- Register and login require a valid email address and a password of at least 8 characters.\n    24\t- Duplicate registration returns `409`.\n    25\t- Invalid login credentials return `401`.\n    26\t- JWT payloads include `userId`.\n    27\t- Authenticated bookmark and folder responses do not include password hashes.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Data Contract\n    30\t\n    31\tBookmark records are stored in SQLite `data.db` in the `bookmarks` table:\n    32\t\n    33\t- `id`: integer primary key\n    34\t- `user_id`: required integer foreign key to `users.id`\n    35\t- `url`: required text\n    36\t- `title`: required text\n    37\t- `description`: nullable text\n    38\t- `folder_id`: nullable integer foreign key to `folders.id`\n    39\t- `created_at`: ISO timestamp text\n    40\t- `updated_at`: ISO timestamp text\n    41\t\n    42\tFolder records are stored in SQLite `data.db` in the `folders` table:\n    43\t\n    44\t- `id`: integer primary key\n    45\t- `user_id`: required integer foreign key to `users.id`\n    46\t- `name`: required text\n    47\t- `created_at`: ISO timestamp text\n    48\t- `updated_at`: ISO timestamp text\n    49\t\n    50\tUser records are stored in SQLite `data.db` in the `users` table:\n    51\t\n    52\t- `id`: integer primary key\n    53\t- `email`: required unique text\n    54\t- `password_hash`: required text\n    55\t- `created_at`: ISO timestamp text\n    56\t\n    57\t## Validation\n    58\t\n    59\t- `url` is required for creation and must be a valid URL.\n    60\t- `url`, when provided on update, must be a non-empty valid URL.\n    61\t- `title` is required for creation and must be a non-empty string after trimming whitespace.\n    62\t- `title`, when provided on update, must be a non-empty string after trimming whitespace.\n    63\t- Empty or whitespace-only titles and URLs are rejected with `400`.\n    64\t- `folder_id`, when provided, must reference an existing folder or the request returns `400`.\n    65\t- `folder_id`, when provided, must reference a folder owned by the authenticated user.\n    66\t- Folder `name` is required for creation and must be a non-empty string after trimming whitespace.\n    67\t- Folder `name`, when provided on update, must be a non-empty string after trimming whitespace.\n    68\t- `email` is required for registration and login and must be a valid email address.\n    69\t- `password` is required for registration and login and must be at least 8 characters.\n    70\t\n    71\t## Pagination\n    72\t\n    73\t- `GET /bookmarks` accepts optional `page` and `limit` query parameters.\n    74\t- `page` defaults to `1` and must be an integer of at least `1`.\n    75\t- `limit` defaults to `20` and must be an integer from `1` through `100`.\n    76\t- Invalid `page` or `limit` values return `400`.\n    77\t- `total` is the authenticated user's full bookmark count before pagination.\n    78\t- `GET /folders/:id` continues to return its folder bookmarks as an unpaginated array.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
