./benchmark/runs/phase-2-observability-taxonomy/T2-crud-bookmarks/events.jsonl:86:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' docs/stories/US-002-crud-bookmarks.md\"","aggregated_output":"# US-002 CRUD Bookmarks\n\n## Status\n\nin_progress\n\n## Lane\n\nnormal\n\n## Product Contract\n\nThe API persists bookmarks in SQLite and exposes create, list, read, update,\nand delete endpoints. Bookmark creation requires a non-empty `url` and\nnon-empty `title`. Health checks continue to return `{ \"status\": \"ok\" }`.\n\n## Relevant Product Docs\n\n- `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- `POST /bookmarks` creates a bookmark and returns `201` with the created row.\n- `GET /bookmarks` returns all bookmarks as an array.\n- `GET /bookmarks/:id` returns the bookmark or `404`.\n- `PUT /bookmarks/:id` updates the bookmark or returns `404`.\n- `DELETE /bookmarks/:id` deletes the bookmark with `204` or returns `404`.\n- Missing or empty required create fields return `400`.\n- `GET /health` still returns `200`.\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Commands: create, update, delete bookmark rows.\n- Queries: list all bookmarks and fetch a single bookmark by id.\n- API: REST endpoints under `/bookmarks`.\n- Tables: `bookmarks`.\n- Domain rules: `url` and `title` are required non-empty strings on create.\n- UI surfaces: none.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Layer | Expected proof |\n| --- | --- |\n| Unit | TypeScript build |\n| Integration | HTTP requests for all bookmark endpoints |\n| E2E | Not required for API-only slice |\n| Platform | SQLite `data.db` contains `bookmarks` table |\n| Release | Not required |\n\n## Harness Delta\n\nNo harness behavior changes expected.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPending validation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
