docs/decisions/0010-folder-sharing-read-only-authorization.md:8:Folder sharing introduces a second access mode for folders and bookmarks. Existing access checks were owner-only and mostly encoded directly in SQL through `user_id = ?` predicates.
docs/decisions/0010-folder-sharing-read-only-authorization.md:12:Folder sharing is modeled as explicit read-only grants in a `folder_shares` table. A user may read a folder when they own it or have an active share for it. A user may write folders, bookmarks, tags, import data, and bookmark-tag assignments only when they own the affected data.
docs/decisions/0010-folder-sharing-read-only-authorization.md:14:Shared users receive 403 for write attempts against resources they can identify through an active share. Users without ownership or a share receive 404 for private folders/bookmarks to avoid leaking private data.
docs/decisions/0010-folder-sharing-read-only-authorization.md:21:- Import/export remain owner-only and do not operate on shared folders.
